    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10500,
      "caption": "Local Exec: the offset from the thread pointer is a link-time constant.",
      "narration": "The fastest model is local exec for executables only. The linker knows the variable's fixed offset from the thread pointer, so access is one fs-relative mov.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Local Exec",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "le",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "asm",
          "text": "movl %fs:x@tpoff, %eax",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "r",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "R_X86_64_TPOFF32. Executable only.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 35.9,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 1900,
          "enter": "fade",
          "color": "green"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl-le",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "le",
          "at": 3600
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "Initial Exec: the offset is loaded from a GOT slot filled at startup.",
      "narration": "For libraries loaded at startup, the offset isn't known at link time. Initial exec loads it from the GOT, then adds it to fs. One extra load.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Initial Exec",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "ie",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "asm",
          "text": "movq x@gottpoff(%rip), %rax\nmovl %fs:(%rax), %eax",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "r",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "R_X86_64_GOTTPOFF. Static TLS block: no dlopen.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 39.8,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 1900,
          "enter": "fade",
          "color": "orange"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl-ie",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "ie",
          "at": 3600
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 12000,
      "caption": "General Dynamic calls __tls_get_addr; Local Dynamic calls it once per module.",
      "narration": "General dynamic works even for dlopen-ed libraries. It passes a module id and offset to __tls_get_addr. Local dynamic calls it once for the module block, then adds offsets.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Dynamic models",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "gd",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "asm",
          "text": "leaq x@tlsgd(%rip), %rdi\ncall __tls_get_addr@PLT",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "ld",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "GD: R_X86_64_TLSGD, per variable",
            "LD: R_X86_64_TLSLD, per module"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 39.8,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 1900,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "red"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 11500,
      "caption": "Pick by scope: -ftls-model=; the linker relaxes GD to IE or LE when it can.",
      "narration": "Shared libraries default to general dynamic with fPIC. When the linker sees the final link context, it can relax these sequences into cheaper initial or local exec ones.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Choosing a model",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "tbl",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Executable: local-exec",
            "Startup libs: initial-exec",
            "dlopen libs: general-dynamic",
            "ld relaxes GD to IE/LE"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "purple"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "takeaway": "TLS models trade generality for speed: more link-time knowledge means fewer instructions per access.",
  "sources": [
    "https://www.akkadia.org/drepper/tls.pdf"
  ]
